    {
      "question": "Does opposite Treasury/Ledger order alone prove payout-versus-cashout deadlock?",
      "answer": "NO. Same employee requests acquire common employeeanchor first, preventing both from progressing into these inner opposite orders simultaneously. Different employees do not share same logical ledger resource. This defeats simple alleged two-node same-employee cycle.",
